<title>SLOVENIA: Daiwa gets go-ahead to buy into two Slovene banks.</title>
<headline>Daiwa gets go-ahead to buy into two Slovene banks.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Slovenia said on Friday it had given the green light to Daiwa Europe to buy 2.94 percent of bank Probanka and 3.51 percent of Dolenjska banka.</p>
<p>&quot;We allowed Daiwa to purchase exactly the amount of shares in both banks as it requested (in May),&quot; the central bank's secretary Matjaz Cepin told Reuters.</p>
<p>According to Slovenian legislation, the central bank must approve any foreign purchase of Slovenian banks.</p>
<p>Daiwa becomes the first foreign shareholder in Probanka and Dolenjska.</p>
<p>-- Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
</text>
